{
  "uid": "individuals-api",
  "title": "individuals-api",
  "description": "Traffic, latency and logs of the external entry layer. Metrics come from Prometheus, logs from Loki; a trace id in a log line links straight to Tempo.",
  "tags": ["payment-platform"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Requests per second, by status",
      "description": "Anything other than 2xx climbing is the first signal that something is wrong.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency, 95th percentile by endpoint",
      "description": "Built from the histogram actuator exposes. The 95th percentile is used rather than the average, which hides exactly the slow requests worth looking at.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{uri}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Registration outcome",
      "description": "The three counters of the registration flow. Attempts counts requests that reached RegistrationService, so a body rejected by @Valid with 400 (Bad Request) never appears here - this panel is the health of the orchestration, not the quality of the input. Attempts standing above success plus failure means registrations are hanging: started, and finished as neither.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(auth_registration_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "attempts"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(auth_registration_success_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "succeeded"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "rate(auth_registration_failure_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Logins and refreshes",
      "description": "Refusals are deliberately not split into a wrong password and a Keycloak that is down: the distinction already lives in the error code and the logs, and a meter carrying it would invite an alert that fires on users mistyping. Refresh has no failure counter at all - an expired refresh token is the normal end of a session, not an incident.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "login attempts"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(auth_login_failure_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "login failures"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "rate(auth_refresh_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "token refreshes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbound calls: is it us, or is it them?",
      "description": "Average duration of one call - summed time divided by call count. The single question it answers: when an endpoint gets slow, did we get slow or did a dependency? Both timers stop on doFinally, so a call that failed still counts; leaving failures out would flatten these lines exactly when something is wrong.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(external_keycloak_requests_seconds_sum[5m]) / rate(external_keycloak_requests_seconds_count[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "keycloak"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(external_person_service_requests_seconds_sum[5m]) / rate(external_person_service_requests_seconds_count[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "person-service"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Since the application started",
      "description": "Raw counter values rather than a rate. After a handful of manual calls a five-minute rate has averaged the burst down to almost nothing, and these read straight. They reset to zero on restart, which is why the panels above ask for a rate instead.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "auth_registration_total",
          "legendFormat": "registrations",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "auth_registration_success_total",
          "legendFormat": "succeeded",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "auth_registration_failure_total",
          "legendFormat": "failed",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "auth_login_total",
          "legendFormat": "logins",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "expr": "auth_login_failure_total",
          "legendFormat": "login failures",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "F",
          "expr": "auth_refresh_total",
          "legendFormat": "refreshes",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Errors and warnings",
      "description": "level is a Loki label, so this filter is answered from the index instead of by scanning bodies.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{service=\"individuals-api\", level=~\"ERROR|WARN\"}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "All logs of the service",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{service=\"individuals-api\"}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
